t_id":"4651-355f-af2a-406a"},{"link_uuid":"69e32141-d95c-46ec-9331-d99316ad6d5a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3f80-99f3-3653-479a"},{"link_uuid":"81df7385-5f6a-4a03-877a-e5ae4126258a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"080e-d303-ed8c-4fa1"},{"link_uuid":"39b56336-cb64-451e-bf72-417c11ce647a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0df6-b4f6-48e6-4acf"},{"link_uuid":"0cac49de-2b8a-492b-a48d-5fa80ee4ca11","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6102-8491-af43-4196"},{"link_uuid":"15d0ce22-d97b-4b4e-9b06-ac7bd16ae9d9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e84c-703d-7877-474b"},{"link_uuid":"da36ec9c-4441-4fec-8c4c-c5b2cd54850c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"39e3-19ae-4308-4f2f"},{"link_uuid":"e4e80cbe-dbc4-43ea-82b5-68fd0d48595e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c813-0b17-6637-4850"},{"link_uuid":"a09631f8-e2e8-4bfc-b987-aca9d36c26d4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fcd0-3e78-28ab-4e78"},{"link_uuid":"3db73327-d017-4104-9282-67be785b17b3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3930-1f6a-2d8b-41ed"},{"link_uuid":"bd323f40-944e-4cf7-9a6b-0946e507be1b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"96b0-81b6-f8fd-4ac6"},{"link_uuid":"26b6563b-e4d6-44b3-9698-5fcd5e8bde86","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"02e3-43b6-de7c-4d24"},{"link_uuid":"49abff8a-8ca3-44aa-8421-98f98a824b61","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7517-791e-1a0f-4783"},{"link_uuid":"1855d303-5eba-42af-81f0-b559ee8ac400","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b87c-6552-f18b-4e68"},{"link_uuid":"bd832f4c-927c-4536-8f46-8aacc857a833","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"73d1-6ff8-6397-4043"},{"link_uuid":"00be89cb-132b-42f0-8da5-52095a89e97b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9edb-7858-955d-4bcb"},{"link_uuid":"e2e9fcbd-ae2b-41b0-8f5c-7011d74cd102","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a3e2-279e-bf7c-4447"},{"link_uuid":"6b22c120-e63a-4bc1-900f-fdeaf2a1da09","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6efa-8369-d057-483e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_store cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/canonical.py:1-48` — Preserve canonical JSON parameters, integer safety, and bytes/string helper roles. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/ensures.py:1-28, 41-74, 153-208` — Preserve stable IDs, locked sweep semantics, incompatibility propagation, and rate-limited pending hint. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py:1-45, 208-263` — Preserve local identity role, loud minting, bounded evidence sample, and author-scoped divergence signal. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:1-35, 110-137, 187-221, 378-418, 455-550` — Preserve lock/atomicity, path-scoped prune, rollback, recoverable conflict rules, and poisoned-index recovery. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py:1-22, 38-77, 87-123, 222-234` — Preserve bounded Git calls, transient/index-lock composition, and explicit maintenance. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py:1-45` — Preserve the freshness predicate, contention posture, and certification consequences. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:1-58` — Preserve atomic-write algorithm, durability limits, permissions, and cleanup guarantees. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py:1-41, 388-465` — Preserve common-directory lock, stale-lock proof, retry bounds, and non-lock failure behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py:1-28, 97-134, 216-235, 303-327` — Preserve closed classification predicates and their subtractive/precedence distinctions. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:1-34, 161-194, 254-334` — Preserve wrapper contract, timeout folding, retry eligibility, watchdog rationale, and foreign-path safety. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:1-40` — Preserve HLC formula, durable-history reseeding, cache role, and integer-serialization warning. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py:1-16, 35-75, 126-200, 303-456` — Preserve stamp format/compatibility, host/process identity, ceiling, and conservative proof rules. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock.py:1-57, 85-118, 225-346, 416-494` — Preserve dual-leg ordering, stale-reclaim proof, holder diagnostics, and retry safety. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/merge_recovery.py:1-31` — Preserve shared recoverable classes, quarantine safety, and caller-specific policy boundary. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/paths.py:1-39, 81-85` — Preserve canonical store-relative derivation and the exact risky construct signature. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:1-24, 76-105, 166-182` — Preserve legacy seeding inputs, idempotence, and multi-project capability-stamp threshold. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:1-7, 48-84, 148-195` — Preserve terminal/retry classifier, jitter schedule, and backlog-growth severity. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py:1-28, 48-109, 250-261, 349-393` — Preserve stack-free stash object, conflict safety, transient retry, and sleep/fetch/merge order. Consumer: `_resolve_conflicted_apply.__doc__` test requires `get_rotation.json`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/canonical.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/freshness.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock_own